From f25db0e2f192bf02c72776e8a82f6a4a2d8f98d5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alex Perrin <44126061+AlexPerrin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 20:37:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the Slayer streak in the OSRS varbits and use OSRS
 wording

- The task streaks now live in the client-visible OSRS varbits
  slayer_tasks_completed (4069) and slayer_wilderness_tasks_completed instead
  of the server-only slayer_streak/slayer_wildy_streak, so client plugins
  (RuneLite's Slayer plugin) can show them.
- The completion message counts the streak, as in OSRS ("You've completed N
  tasks ...", "N Wilderness tasks" for Krystilia).
- The gem check says "You're assigned to kill X; only N more to go." (Konar:
  "kill X in Area"), the wording client plugins parse.
Adds an integration test suite to content/skills/slayer with SlayerTaskVarsTest.
